137
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:03,280
And I had this comment from Larry Geiger.

138
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:06,020
I, like you, like a specified ceremony.

139
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:08,280
But the scouts usually want something else.

140
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:10,560
So off they go, Googling and writing.

141
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:14,600
And I never know exactly what's going to happen until it happens.

142
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:18,900
If you're a Scoutmaster and you have a significant role in your court of honor, or you're nervous

143
00:09:18,900 --> 00:09:22,240
about how it's going to go in your role in it, then you're over-involved.

144
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:23,580
That's a good rule of thumb, Larry.

145
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:25,440
If you're nervous, you're over-involved.

146
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,700
That's not bad.

147
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:31,280
Like camping, this is one thing the scouts can do and do well.

148
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:35,460
Nothing puts boys on alert like getting up in front of a crowd.

149
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:39,620
Last night, I was throwing away a bunch of stuff, and I found an old court of honor agenda

150
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,280
