151
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:45,200
He left it on the podium, and I had picked it up on my way out the door and shoved it

152
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,040
into my notebook.

153
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:48,120
It was something he got off the internet.

154
00:09:48,340 --> 00:09:52,820
Basically, he printed it out and then just marked all over it and scribbled some stuff

155
00:09:52,820 --> 00:09:54,400
out and renumbered things.

156
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,439
It was a real mess.

157
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:59,720
I don't know how he followed it, but he did just fine.

158
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:03,800
If I had more space, I would frame it and put it up in our meeting room.

159
00:10:04,060 --> 00:10:05,819
And, Larry, I couldn't agree with you more.

160
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:09,959
That is a fantastic approach to courts of honor and just about anything else in scouting.

161
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,180
Go to the scouts.

162
00:10:11,439 --> 00:10:12,520
What do you want to do, fellas?

163
00:10:12,939 --> 00:10:14,240
How do you want to handle this?

164
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,319
How do you want to manage it?

165
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:17,199
And you'll be amazed with the results.

166
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:18,800
That's for sure.

